<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sun En</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 402</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sun En was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/way-of-the-five-pecks-of-rice">Five Pecks of Rice</a> Daoist sect who led a great rebellion along the south-east coast of Eastern Jin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 399. His seaborne forces threatened the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a> before being repelled; he drowned himself in 402. Suppressing the revolt raised the general Liu Yu, who founded the Liu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> in 420.</p></div>
